{
  "_doc": "Features painted into original facade textures, in the texture's own pixels (x right, y down from the top-left of build/textures/<grd>.png). tools/blender/build_zone_art.py rebuilds them as geometry wherever a wall uses the texture: openings are cut and recessed (glass/door panel at the back keeps the painted image), frame_px wide surrounds, bands (horizontal) and piers (vertical) stand proud of the wall, crenels become solid merlons, roofs get thickness and overhangs. Timber framing and masonry relief come from Nanite displacement instead (height modes in tools/textures/make_placeholders.py, strengths in materials.json). Check alignment with: python tools/environment/facades.py. Sizes in metres; 'trim' names the texture used for reveals and the stone faces the painting doesn't cover.",
